\description{
Turn per-crop harvested-derived physical area into a fallow-inclusive physical
land extension whose arable-crop total reconciles to FAO's physical
\strong{Arable land} and whose perennial-crop total reconciles to FAO's physical
\strong{Permanent crops} (\code{\link[=get_arable_permanent_land]{get_arable_permanent_land()}}), per \verb{(area_code, year)}.

This is the FAO-land-base analogue of \code{\link[=build_cropgrids_land_extension]{build_cropgrids_land_extension()}}\code{(source = "cropgrids_fallow")}. The existing method takes the fallow \emph{magnitude} from
FAOSTAT "Temporary fallow" (item 6640, a sparse and, for many rain-fed
economies, absent series) applied to a single CROPGRIDS 2020 snapshot. Here
the fallow magnitude is the physical arable land that carried no harvest in
that specific year, \verb{FAO Arable land - sum(cropped arable physical)}, so a
drought year's resting cropland is charged to the crops whose rotation it
supports and the arable-crop footprint totals match FAO's land survey in every
year (see the Tunisia/Portugal motivation in \code{\link[=get_arable_permanent_land]{get_arable_permanent_land()}}).

Reconciliation, per \verb{(area_code, year)}:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Arable crops} (\code{items_prod_full$Herb_Woody != "Woody"}): rotational
fallow \code{max(0, arable_ha - S)} (with \code{S} the cropped arable physical total)
is distributed with \code{\link[=attribute_fallow_to_crops]{attribute_fallow_to_crops()}} using \code{fallow_weights}, so
the arable total reaches \code{arable_ha}. Where the cropped physical already
exceeds \code{arable_ha} (heavy multi-cropping, or inflated fodder harvested
area) there is no fallow to add and the arable crops are scaled down to
\code{arable_ha} instead, the physical-container correction. Either way the
arable total equals FAO \code{arable_ha} by construction.
\item \strong{Perennial crops} (\code{Herb_Woody == "Woody"}) receive no fallow and are
scaled so their total equals FAO \code{permanent_ha}, preserving the within-group
physical pattern.
A positive target without a corresponding arable crop row or positive
perennial base area is reported as an error because it cannot be reconciled
without inventing a crop allocation.
}

This is the crop-side default of the land-balance footprint
(\code{\link[=build_land_balance_footprint]{build_land_balance_footprint()}}).
